cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "EndoTarget Evidence: cross-study target prioritization in endometriosis using donor-level transcriptomics and network analysis"
abstract: >-
  Public-data endometriosis target-evidence benchmark. Donor-level pseudobulk
  modeling of proliferative-phase eutopic endometrial stromal fibroblasts in
  two public single-cell cohorts (GSE266265 discovery, HECA E-MTAB-14039
  external), expression ranking against two network baselines on a frozen
  STRING functional-association graph, external-cohort evaluation of frozen
  lists, a separate genetic-evidence layer, and verified Nextflow/Docker
  reproduction. The completed analysis found no statistically supported
  cross-study target shortlist and no advantage for network propagation.
  Prespecified follow-on analyses (October 2026) add a cycle-phase positive
  control, minimum-detectable-effect bounds, a secretory-phase program-level
  disease contrast and a public-cohort extension audit.
